# Shop

The online shop allows your members to order additional products from their account a few days before the delivery of their next <%= Basket.model_name.human(count: 2).downcase %>.

Two switches. First, disable the admin-only limitation in [the settings](/settings#shop) so the shop appears in the member menu. Then [open the shop on deliveries](#opening). Products do not show in the member account until both are done. Complements on a membership are not the shop.

## Producers {#producers}

Each product can be associated with [a producer](/shop_producers). A description as well as a link to a website or document can be defined for each of them. All products can be filtered by producer in the member interface of the shop.

## Products {#products}

Many options are offered to best manage the products of your shop.

### Tags {#tags}

[Tags](/shop_tags) are keywords that allow filtering products in the member interface of the shop. Each product can be associated with one or more tags.

### Variants

Each product comes in one or more variants. Variants allow defining different characteristics (weight, size, type) of this product.

Each variant has its own name, price, weight (optional), and stock (optional).

### Availability

The availability of a product can be defined for itself or for each of its variants separately. If needed, a product can also be made unavailable by depot or for a future delivery.

> If the stock of a variant is defined and falls to zero, it will still appear but it will simply no longer be possible to add it to the shopping cart.

### Complements

Each product variant can be linked to one existing [<%= BasketComplement.model_name.human.downcase %>](/handbook/deliveries#basket-complements). Orders for a linked variant add its quantity to that complement in the summary (XLSX) and sheets (PDF) of the <%= Basket.model_name.human.downcase %> delivery.

One product can therefore group variants linked to different complement choices. Each linked variant is available only on its complement's delivery days; other variants retain their own availability.

## Orders {#orders}

To give you time to process and bill orders placed before delivery, a deadline (days and hours) until which orders are possible can be defined from [the shop settings](/settings#shop). After this deadline, members will no longer be able to create or modify their order for the upcoming delivery.

It's also possible to set a minimum order amount as well as a maximum weight, if this information has been properly entered for each product variant.

Once an order is placed, it appears with the status "to prepare" in [the orders list](/shop_orders?scope=pending). These orders are always modifiable by members until the configured deadline. An admin can also modify them at any time.

A delivery note (PDF), not including the price of products, is available for each order if you wish to print them and attach them to the <%= Basket.model_name.human(count: 2).downcase %>.

### Billing {#billing}

By default, once the orders are prepared, the orders must be **manually** billed (possibility to bill them all at once via a group action). The invoice is then automatically sent by email to the member.

It's also possible to configure **automatic billing** of orders, from [the shop settings](/settings#shop), after or before a certain number of days following or preceding the delivery date.

> If you modify an order that has already been billed, its existing invoice is automatically canceled. Generate and send a new invoice.

It's possible to add specific text in the ["New invoice" email template](/mail_templates/invoice_created) using [Liquid syntax](https://shopify.github.io/liquid) as follows:

~~~ liquid
{% case invoice.entity_type %}
{% when 'Shop::Order' %}
  <p>Here is your new invoice for order No. {{ invoice.entity_number }}; all details can be found in the attached PDF.</p>
{% else %}
  <p>Here is your new invoice; all details can be found in the attached PDF.</p>
{% endcase %}
~~~

### Price flexibility {#price-flexibility}

If you want to let members voluntarily adjust the price of their orders (as a solidarity contribution or a discount), you can define a list of percentages in [the shop settings](/settings#shop). For example: `-10, -5, 5, 10`.

When percentages are configured, members see a dropdown on the order page where they can apply an adjustment (e.g. "Support +10%" or "Discount -5%"). This adjustment applies to the total order amount. If the list contains only positive values, the label reads as a support contribution; if only negative, as a discount.

## Terms of sale {#terms-of-sale}

A link to your terms of sale can be configured per language in [the shop settings](/settings#shop). When set, the link is displayed at the bottom of the member shop page.

## Access for members without membership {#access-without-membership}

By default, and outside of [special deliveries](#special-deliveries), access to the shop is limited to active members with a membership. However, it's possible to define a depot, by modifying the profile of an inactive member, as a "shop depot" to give them access to the shop. Orders from these members will then appear in the sheets (PDF) of the corresponding depots.

A delivery cycle can also be assigned to limit which deliveries are accessible in the shop for these members. Without a delivery cycle, all deliveries where the shop is open for the assigned depot will be available.

### Example: restaurants or professional buyers {#restaurants}

A common use case is to give access to the shop to restaurants or other professional buyers who don't have a membership. Here's how to set this up:

1. **Create a hidden depot** specifically for these members (e.g. "Restaurants"). Since it's not visible to regular members, it won't clutter the depot list during sign-up.
2. **Assign this depot as the "shop depot"** on each restaurant member's profile.
3. **Limit product visibility using depot availability**: by making certain products unavailable for all depots _except_ this restaurant depot, you can offer a catalog exclusively reserved for these professional buyers (e.g. larger formats, bulk pricing). Regular members with a membership will not see these products.
4. **Control shop opening per depot**: when opening the shop on a delivery, you can select only the restaurant depot. This way, the shop remains closed for members with a membership on that delivery while being open for restaurants. Conversely, you can open the shop for all depots when you want everyone to have access.
5. **Assign a delivery cycle** (optional): if restaurants should only order on specific delivery dates, assign a matching delivery cycle to further restrict their available deliveries.

> These members are best created manually by an admin via the [member creation form](/members/new), since the registration form focuses on standard members who will also take a membership.

## Special deliveries {#special-deliveries}

Special deliveries allow you to offer additional products to your members outside of regular <%= Basket.model_name.human.downcase %> deliveries via the online shop.

Available products can be defined separately for each special delivery, the individual setting of the availability of each product is ignored. However, the availability of variants as well as the state of their stock are always respected.

> As special deliveries are delivered outside of <%= Basket.model_name.human.downcase %> deliveries, they are open to all your members, active or not.

## Opening the shop {#opening}

Before members can place orders, the shop must be **opened on the desired deliveries** from [the deliveries page](/deliveries). This can be done in batches using the "Open shop" group action, or individually by editing a delivery (where you can also select specific depots). The shop can be closed again the same way if needed.

Members with only a shop depot are [active](/handbook/members#statuses) because of that depot. They receive [Member activated](/mail_templates/member_activated) unless you use [Shop access activated](/mail_templates/member_shop_depot_activated).
